-### DON'T: Use innerHTML when replacing a named target
-```typescript
-// WRONG — innerHTML replaces children, losing the target element's id
-// Subsequent swaps to the same target will fail because the id is gone
-hx("/users", { target: ids.userList, swap: "innerHTML" })
-
-// CORRECT — outerHTML replaces the element itself (re-renders the id)
-hx("/users", { target: ids.userList, swap: "outerHTML show:window:top" })
-```
+No htmx runtime is served here: hx-* attributes are inert and `template/no-htmx-without-runtime`
+fails lint on them. Forms post and links navigate natively; a failed submit is a full-page 400:
+- `Form(...).setAction(contactRoutes.submit.resolve()).setMethod("post")`
+- `A(post.title).setHref(blogRoutes.post.resolve({ slug: post.slug }))`
 
